# playcric365 GAMEPLAY (Baccarat) bot: the casino/hedge commands
# (/testbaccarat, /pair, /pairs, /delpair, /run, /stoprun, /runs, /runlog)
# driving Evolution Baccarat on playcric365.com -- acc1 always bets Banker,
# acc2 always bets Player on the SAME hand at the SAME table, so the money
# mostly moves between the two accounts and only the ~5% banker commission
# bleeds. Same engine as the cricmatch/winclash gameplay bots. No signup
# commands -- those live on .env.playcric365.signup.
#
# NO CAPSOLVER KEY NEEDED. playcric365 has no WAF at all: a bare request to
# "/" answers 200 with an ordinary Laravel session. Unlike winclash, nothing
# here has to solve a challenge, so seats cost no CapSolver credit.
#
# WHAT IS CONFIRMED (2026-10-22, read-only over plain HTTP -- no account, no
# bet, nothing registered):
#   * This site is the same white-label Laravel platform as cricmatch247 /
#     khelofun / starexch555, and its live-casino lobby uses starexch's
#     vocabulary: tiles are div[onclick="goToCasinoLive(this)"] and the
#     provider lives in the lobby URL (/live-casino?p=evolution).
#   * The site's own catalogue endpoint (POST /displaygames, game=baccarat)
#     lists, under provider "evolution":
#         Baccarat A = data-id 85     Baccarat B = data-id 86
#     which are the SAME ids starexch uses, as a shared template predicts.
#   * The login markup is cricmatch's byte for byte, fetched on demand from
#     /append/loginpp (so it is absent from the homepage source -- don't
#     conclude the selectors are wrong by grepping the page).
#
# WHAT IS *NOT* VERIFIED, and it matters before any real money:
#   * NOTHING BEHIND THE LOGIN HAS EVER BEEN DRIVEN ON THIS SITE. No account
#     was available during mapping, and logged out the site's own
#     goToCasinoLive() is stubbed to just open the login modal, so the real
#     tile-launch handler could not even be read. The route in
#     sites/playcric365.py is starexch's pair (direct_url + go_to_casino_live)
#     because the markup matches starexch's -- not because a table was opened.
#   * NO BET HAS EVER BEEN PLACED HERE.
#   * THE TABLE MINIMUM IS UNKNOWN. Baccarat A is 100 rupees a side on every
#     other site in this family, so 100 is the likely figure -- but do not
#     assume it. The chip rail is read live by the probe below.
#   * This site also carries an EZUGI-client baccarat (data-provider="ezugi",
#     e.g. "Casino Marina Baccarat B") whose markup this engine CANNOT drive.
#     That is exactly why casino_lobby_path pins ?p=evolution. If a run ever
#     lands somewhere the bet spots don't exist, check the provider first.
#
# So, in order, before any real money:
#   1. .venv/bin/python verify_baccarat.py <user> <pass> --url https://playcric365.com/
#      Read-only, places NO bets. Prints the table id (a wrong id opens some
#      other table perfectly happily), both bet spots, the real chip rail
#      (i.e. the true minimum stake) and counts betting windows.
#   2. /testbaccarat <user> <pass> 100
#      Confirms login + lobby + a real table + a real placement, and reports
#      the actual TOTAL BET. This one DOES stake real money.
#   3. /run <pair> <table minimum> 1   -- ONE round -- then read /runlog.
# Only scale the amount or the rounds after step 3 settles cleanly.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=your-playcric365-gameplay-bot-token-from-botfather
# One id, or several comma-/space-separated ids for multiple master admins:
# MASTER_ADMIN_ID=111111111,222222222
MASTER_ADMIN_ID=your-telegram-user-id

CAPSOLVER_API_KEY=

BOT_MODE=gameplay
BOT_SITE_URL=https://playcric365.com
ADMINS_FILE=admins.playcric365.gameplay.json
SETTINGS_FILE=bot_settings.playcric365.gameplay.json
ADMIN_PHONES_FILE=admin_phones.playcric365.gameplay.json
# Pair credentials + run history. MUST be distinct from every other
# instance's files -- each process reads them once at import and rewrites
# them whole on every save, so two bots sharing a path silently clobber
# each other. (pairs.* holds plaintext passwords; both patterns are
# gitignored.)
PAIRS_FILE=pairs.playcric365.gameplay.json
PAIR_RUNS_FILE=pair_runs.playcric365.gameplay.json

# How many /run hedge sessions may execute at once (each drives two Chromium
# browsers). Default 3.
# MAX_CONCURRENT_RUNS=3

# NOTE: /freenum is a gameplay-mode command but playcric365 has no
# free-number endpoint (supports_free_number=False), so it refuses cleanly
# rather than mis-firing. Nothing to configure.
